# Line endings are a property of the repository, not of whoever cloned it.
#
# This tree has shell scripts (`microvm/*.sh`, run as PID 1 and under `sudo`),
# a Python demo, Rust sources and a PowerShell script. A CRLF checkout of a
# shell script fails on Linux with `bad interpreter: ...\r`, which is exactly
# the kind of deploy-time surprise that an "it built on my machine" repo
# produces. Normalising to LF on checkout removes the question.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Anything the build treats as opaque bytes stays opaque.
*.ext4   binary
*.snap   binary
*.gguf   binary
*.vmlinux binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.ico    binary
